<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9841] SQL doesn&apos;t take lost partitions into account when persistence is enabled</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9841</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8927&quot; title=&quot;Hangs when executing an SQL query when there are LOST partitions&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-8927&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-8927&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; changed SQL queries to honor lost partitions. However, it doesn&apos;t work if persistence is enabled. E.g. if there are lost partitions then `select * from T` fails for in-memory caches (good) and silently ignores the lost partitions for persistent caches (bad).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See attached reproducer.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
